# lowered from the probe strings.json by the fixture lowering (private tooling)
# The lane runs `ds-formal-tests --fixture` on this and diffs against
# strings.expected (scripts/formal/check_idris.py). The real-strings rung's
# smoke pair: nine S facts with a String slot txt (payload
# 0) and an Int slot n (payload 1), one rule per reading. The fixture reads
# texts, so the lowering writes a `string` record for every token of its
# table before the rules: 0 M, 1 abc, 2 é (the rules' literals, in rule
# order), then the steps' values in slot order -- 3 a, 4 Z, 5 b, 6 ab, 7 c,
# 8 0x1F, 9 d, 10 3_1, 11 e, 12 true, 13 f, 14 g, 15 h, 16 31_, 17 i,
# 18 -0x1F (é and abc already minted). An ordering on two Strings is
# lexicographic by codepoint (rules 0 and 1, [LSTR.3.2]); `slen` counts
# codepoints (2, [LSTR.2.1]); `cast int 1` parses 0x1F and 3_1 to 31 and
# -0x1F to -31 and is null of every other text, 31_'s trailing separator
# included (3, 4 and 7, [LCST.4.5.7], [LLEX.12.1]); `cast bool 1` parses
# true (5, [LCST.4.5.5]); equality is codepoint by codepoint (6, [LSTR.3.1]).
# The renders of [LCST.4.5.6] are not probed here (the compiler lowers them,
# FN_INT_TO_STRING / FN_BOOL_TO_STRING; the vectors are
# logical/LCST.4.5.6_*). The keys are the
# codes of the nine entity ids (8 * token + 3: 27, 43, 59, 75, 91, 107, 115,
# 123, 139) and the payloads the codes of (txt, n): a String is 8 * token + 3
# and an Int n is 8 * zigzag(n) + 2.
schema 0 entity S
alpha 0 0
string 0 1 77
string 1 3 97 98 99
string 2 1 233
string 3 1 97
string 4 1 90
string 5 1 98
string 6 2 97 98
string 7 1 99
string 8 4 48 120 49 70
string 9 1 100
string 10 3 51 95 49
string 11 1 101
string 12 4 116 114 117 101
string 13 1 102
string 14 1 103
string 15 1 104
string 16 3 51 49 95
string 17 1 105
string 18 5 45 48 120 49 70
rule 0 gt_m
pattern 0 0 0
where 0 0 gt slot 0 pay 0 lit s:0
log 0 0 0
rule 1 prefix_first
pattern 1 0 0
where 1 0 lt slot 0 pay 0 lit s:1
log 1 0 0
rule 2 len_two
pattern 2 0 0
where 2 0 eq slen slot 0 pay 0 lit i:2
log 2 0 0
rule 3 parses_31
pattern 3 0 0
where 3 0 eq coalesce cast int 1 slot 0 pay 0 lit i:0 lit i:31
log 3 0 0
rule 4 parse_null
pattern 4 0 0
where 4 0 is null cast int 1 slot 0 pay 0
log 4 0 0
rule 5 bool_true
pattern 5 0 0
where 5 0 coalesce cast bool 1 slot 0 pay 0 lit b:0
log 5 0 0
rule 6 equal
pattern 6 0 0
where 6 0 eq slot 0 pay 0 lit s:2
log 6 0 0
rule 7 parses_neg
pattern 7 0 0
where 7 0 eq add coalesce cast int 1 slot 0 pay 0 lit i:0 lit i:31 lit i:0
log 7 0 0
step assert _0 0 1000000000000000000027 1000000000000000000035000000000000000000674
step assert _1 0 1000000000000000000043 1000000000000000000051000000000000000000018
step assert _2 0 1000000000000000000059 1000000000000000000067000000000000000000002
step assert _3 0 1000000000000000000075 1000000000000000000083000000000000000000114
step assert _4 0 1000000000000000000091 1000000000000000000099000000000000000000034
step assert _5 0 1000000000000000000107 1000000000000000000019000000000000000000050
step assert _6 0 1000000000000000000115 1000000000000000000011000000000000000000066
step assert _7 0 1000000000000000000123 1000000000000000000131000000000000000000082
step assert _8 0 1000000000000000000139 1000000000000000000147000000000000000000098
step pump
